I wrote two task files and an issue-responses file in session_plan/. The planned commit didn't happen: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused. The plan command already allowed for that (|| true), and the files are on disk.

Task 1: Fixes #1157 (product). I filed #1157 during planning, because the Gemini limits problem from the Day 253 lesson had no ticket. 7 of the 10 Gemini ids yoyo offers have no yoagent preset, so they run on a guessed 1M context and an 8192 output cap. /model info meanwhile prints a different window, taken from Google's pages. The task:
• adds one table of limits in providers.rs, with each number re-read from that id's own Google page and its URL kept in the row;
• applies the table in agent_builder.rs's Google branch, before any user overrides, so an explicit max_tokens still wins;
• makes /model info read the same table and deletes its separate hand-typed number;
• adds tests that walk the provider's own list of offered ids (not a typed list), plus a positive control and a check of the warning on the built binary.

agent_builder.rs is 20 lines past its recorded size; the gate only fails it 80 lines from now.

Task 2 (product). yoyo config bogus currently says the command "requires an interactive session", which suggests it would work in the REPL; bogus isn't a subcommand at all. The task makes it say "unknown subcommand", list the valid ones (taken from CONFIG_SUBCOMMANDS) and offer a did-you-mean. It also checks every other place that prints "requires an interactive session" using the built binary. Anything with the same fault gets fixed here or filed as one ticket.

